<section id="framework">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">The Framework</div>
    <h2>Product Adoption is a Core Technical Process</h2>

    <div class="purple-squirrel-box">
      <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        A 400 Bad Request error or a UI drop-off is a structural failure in the system's
        onboarding architecture — not a user deficiency. We fix the architecture to match
        human behavior.
      </p>

      <div class="venn-diagram">
        <div class="venn-item">
          <div class="venn-title">Churn Signals</div>
          <div class="venn-desc">
            Users don't leave because they hate your product. They leave because
            your product never gave them a clear path to value. Every abandoned
            signup, skipped step, or support ticket is a measurable data point
            in your friction map.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="venn-item">
          <div class="venn-title">Onboarding Architecture</div>
          <div class="venn-desc">
            The onboarding flow is not a UX concern — it is a systems engineering
            problem. Cognitive load, information sequencing, and error recovery
            paths must be designed with the same rigor as your database schema.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="venn-item">
          <div class="venn-title">Revenue Protection</div>
          <div class="venn-desc">
            User attrition is a revenue event. Every percentage point of improved
            activation rate compounds into LTV. We treat friction removal as a
            direct investment with a measurable ROI, not a usability nicety.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="intersection-note">
        The diagnosis starts where your analytics end — in the behavioral gap between
        what your logs record and what your users actually experience.
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      The backend contracts that keep erratic real-user behavior from contaminating your
      production database and breaking your LLM integrations are documented in full detail.
      <a href="/resilient-infrastructure" style="color: var(--orange-light); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(233,84,32,0.3);">
        [Read the technical specification on Chaos-Tolerant Infrastructure]
      </a>
    </p>

    <div class="adr-quote">
      Live B2C evidence: high-friction user retention engineering applied to a production
      language learning platform serving real users since 2022.<br/>
      <a href="https://huhugerman.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="project-link" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; display: inline-flex;">
        [ Live Lab B2C Case Study: High-Friction User Retention ] →
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
